 - The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
-- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and is passed the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit under-counts every turn that ran tools.
+
+## Usage reporting
+
+- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits, and the usage it receives is summed across every provider call of the turn: a turn driven through two tool rounds reports both rounds' usage, not only the last round's ([validated by: reports usage summed across every provider call of a two-round tool turn](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L66)).
+- A round that reports no usage does not turn the turn's usage into `undefined` or `NaN`: the rounds that reported are still counted ([validated by: counts the rounds that reported when a middle round reports no usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L83)).
+- A turn in which no provider call reported usage reports no usage at all ([validated by: reports no usage when no round of the turn reported any](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L100)).
+- A turn that ran no tools reports exactly what it reported before the turn total existed — the single provider call's usage ([validated by: receives collected response text and usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L236)).
